- The name is used exactly as written. A naming policy doesn't convert it.
- When reading, the document element must have this name, matched with case, or the serializer throws an `XmlException`. `PropertyNameCaseInsensitive` doesn't apply to the document element.
- The attribute names the type as a document element. When the type is the type of a member of another object, the element is named after that member.
- When `Namespace` is `null`, `XmlSerializerOptions.DefaultNamespace` is used.
- The serializer doesn't read `IsNullable`. A `null` reference at the root is written as the document element marked `xsi:nil="true"` whatever its value.
